# Rank 1772 / CVE-2020-13957 (SOLR-14663, CWE-306):
# apache/solr's ConfigSets API dispatches each action to an enum constant of
# ConfigSetsHandler.ConfigSetOperation overriding `call` (an anonymous
# class body per constant). The CREATE constant
# (solr/core/src/java/org/apache/solr/handler/admin/ConfigSetsHandler.java:272
# at the parent) reads the request-controlled `baseConfigSet` parameter and
# returns props the overseer applies by copying that base configset into a
# new one -- with no authentication anywhere in the body. The UPLOAD action
# does authenticate: `getTrusted(req)` (the same file, :191) returns true only
# when `authcPlugin != null && req.getUserPrincipal() != null`, and the
# configset's trust flag decides whether its config may declare executable
# components (RunExecutableListener et al). An unauthenticated CREATE from a
# trusted base produced a configset that inherited nothing of the base's root
# node (the `{"trusted": ...}` marker is never copied) and so landed with the
# permissive default, handing an unauthenticated caller the trusted-configset
# path to arbitrary component execution.
#
# e001c2221812a0ba9e9378855040ce72f93eced4 (SOLR-14663) fixes it inside the
# same enum-constant body: CREATE_OP.call gains
#
#   if (!DISABLE_CREATE_AUTH_CHECKS &&
#           !isTrusted(req, h.coreContainer.getAuthenticationPlugin()) &&
#           isCurrentlyTrusted(h.coreContainer.getZkController().getZkClient(),
#                              ZkConfigManager.CONFIGS_ZKNODE + "/" + baseConfigSetName)) {
#     throw new SolrException(ErrorCode.UNAUTHORIZED, ...);
#   }
#
# plus existence checks on the new and base names, and ZkConfigManager.copyConfigDir
# now copies the base's root node data so the trust flag propagates. The
# remediation is present at the commit and absent at its parent a50c10843, so
# both halves of the 1390 check hold and the pool row is correct in every
# field; no correction needed.
#
# What fires today. `timeout 180 ./bin/vyql scan --cache off --max-ram 6GB`
# over solr/core/src/java/org/apache/solr/handler/admin at both revisions,
# three runs per side, reports byte-identical output: 8 findings and 34 flags
# each (3 at or above high), and `scan -flags only` likewise identical. Not
# one finding or flag lands in ConfigSetsHandler.java on either side -- the
# subtree's rows are SolrInfoMBeanHandler/ZookeeperStatusHandler XSS and
# resource noise. Findings in the file would not be coverage anyway; there are
# none.
#
# The blocker is the Java anonymous-body extraction gap, in its enum-constant
# form. jvConv.stmt (internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/java.go:138) handles
# class/interface/enum/record declarations but has no case for `enum_constant`,
# and c.decls feeds every named child of the enum body to that switch, whose
# default returns nil -- so a constant-specific body, and every method it
# declares, produces no FuncDef, no call nodes and no context tokens. The
# sibling anonymous form is the same: jvConv.expr's `object_creation_expression`
# case (java.go:1241) lowers the constructor and its arguments but ignores the
# trailing `class_body` field. Measured with a probe file holding the identical
# `req.getParameter("x")` call in an enum-constant body and in an ordinary
# method of the same class: `vyql match` labels only the ordinary method
# (code.HttpInput, java.input@syntactic), and `vyql graph` shows the enum
# constant contributing zero nodes -- case (d) below pins this pair. This is
# the gap ranks 1230 and 1260 filed for anonymous classes; the enum-constant
# form reaches it without an `new` anywhere in sight.
#
# The 1380 counterweight cannot be exercised. The fixed revision does leave an
# API-documented call inside the method it guards --
# `h.coreContainer.getAuthenticationPlugin()` is inline in CREATE_OP.call --
# but that method has no node, so no function-scoped binding can key on it.
# Nor can a class-scope binding discriminate: `req.getUserPrincipal()` is
# present in the named (extracted) code of BOTH revisions -- in `getTrusted`
# at the parent, in the static `isTrusted` at the fixed revision -- so any text-level
# negation over the class body fires identically before and after. The only
# extracted code that differs between the revisions is the fixed revision's own new
# symbols (`isTrusted`, `isCurrentlyTrusted`, the
# `solr.disableConfigSetsCreateAuthChecks` property read), which a binding
# must not key on. Both the weakness and its remediation live entirely inside
# the unextracted construct: a double miss with no revision-discriminating
# fact available in any layer.
#
# Not judged mechanical. Lowering enum-constant bodies would add facts to
# every Java scan that has one: 119 sites across 11 of the 1347 files in
# solr/core/src/java alone, 919 sites across 137 of the 98,997 Java files in
# the rank clones under /tmp/cve-work/rank*/, plus the anonymous-class form in
# 169 solr-core files. New FuncDefs mean new function contexts that existing
# presence bindings start matching inside, so the change moves findings on
# trees that have nothing to do with this weakness -- a scan-wide behavior
# change, not a confined correction to a known construct. Unsure = not
# mechanical.
#
# The four cases: (a) and (b) are the two real revisions and record the double
# miss; (c) is the same vulnerable body as (a) written as a named method,
# holding the fact that even the extracted form fires nothing today -- marking
# a config-mutating admin action as requiring an authenticated principal is a
# vocabulary decision that cannot be made keying on this fix's layout, and is
# only worth making once the body is visible at all; (d) is the frontend pair
# isolating the construct, using a servlet request read that an existing
# binding labels (java.input@syntactic on getParameter) so the asymmetry is
# observable in today's output.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap, all four cases rejected. (b)
# is correct code and must remain a reject; (a) and (c) flip to expect only
# once enum-constant bodies lower into FuncDefs AND a binding marks the
# configset-create action as an operation requiring authentication.

test "rank1772: (a) the ConfigSets CREATE action body reads the request-controlled base configset and performs no authenticated-principal check, so an unauthenticated request creates a trusted-derived configset"
  lang java
  file solr/core/src/java/org/apache/solr/handler/admin/ConfigSetsHandler.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-001
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.solr.handler.admin;

  import java.util.Map;
  import org.apache.solr.common.params.SolrParams;
  import org.apache.solr.request.SolrQueryRequest;
  import org.apache.solr.response.SolrQueryResponse;

  public class ConfigSetsHandler {
    protected void invokeAction(SolrQueryRequest req, SolrQueryResponse rsp, String action) throws Exception {
      ConfigSetOperation operation = ConfigSetOperation.get(action);
      Map<String, Object> result = operation.call(req, rsp, this);
    }

    static Map<String, Object> copyPropertiesWithPrefix(SolrParams params, Map<String, Object> props, String prefix) {
      // The configset created via an API should be mutable.
      props.put("immutable", "false");
      return props;
    }

    enum ConfigSetOperation {
      CREATE_OP("create") {
        @Override
        Map<String, Object> call(SolrQueryRequest req, SolrQueryResponse rsp, ConfigSetsHandler h) throws Exception {
          String baseConfigSetName = req.getParams().get("baseConfigSet", "_default");
          Map<String, Object> props = CollectionsHandler.copy(req.getParams().required(), null, "name");
          props.put("baseConfigSet", baseConfigSetName);
          return copyPropertiesWithPrefix(req.getParams(), props, "property.");
        }
      },
      DELETE_OP("delete") {
        @Override
        Map<String, Object> call(SolrQueryRequest req, SolrQueryResponse rsp, ConfigSetsHandler h) throws Exception {
          return CollectionsHandler.copy(req.getParams().required(), null, "name");
        }
      };

      String action;
      ConfigSetOperation(String action) { this.action = action; }
      abstract Map<String, Object> call(SolrQueryRequest req, SolrQueryResponse rsp, ConfigSetsHandler h) throws Exception;
      static ConfigSetOperation get(String action) { return CREATE_OP; }
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1772: (b) the fixed revision rejects an unauthenticated CREATE from a trusted base inside the same enum-constant body"
  lang java
  file solr/core/src/java/org/apache/solr/handler/admin/ConfigSetsHandler.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-001
  reject VYQL-AUTH-079
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.solr.handler.admin;

  import java.util.Map;
  import org.apache.solr.common.SolrException;
  import org.apache.solr.common.cloud.ZkConfigManager;
  import org.apache.solr.common.params.SolrParams;
  import org.apache.solr.request.SolrQueryRequest;
  import org.apache.solr.response.SolrQueryResponse;

  public class ConfigSetsHandler {
    final static boolean DISABLE_CREATE_AUTH_CHECKS = Boolean.getBoolean("solr.disableConfigSetsCreateAuthChecks");

    static class CoreContainer {
      Object getAuthenticationPlugin() { return null; }
      Object getZkController() { return null; }
    }

    static boolean isTrusted(SolrQueryRequest req, Object authPlugin) {
      if (authPlugin != null && req.getUserPrincipal() != null) {
        return true;
      }
      return false;
    }

    static boolean isCurrentlyTrusted(Object zkClient, String configSetZkPath) {
      return true;
    }

    protected void invokeAction(SolrQueryRequest req, SolrQueryResponse rsp, String action) throws Exception {
      ConfigSetOperation operation = ConfigSetOperation.get(action);
      Map<String, Object> result = operation.call(req, rsp, this);
    }

    static Map<String, Object> copyPropertiesWithPrefix(SolrParams params, Map<String, Object> props, String prefix) {
      props.put("immutable", "false");
      return props;
    }

    enum ConfigSetOperation {
      CREATE_OP("create") {
        @Override
        Map<String, Object> call(SolrQueryRequest req, SolrQueryResponse rsp, ConfigSetsHandler h) throws Exception {
          String baseConfigSetName = req.getParams().get("baseConfigSet", "_default");
          String newConfigSetName = req.getParams().get("name");
          if (newConfigSetName == null || newConfigSetName.length() == 0) {
            throw new SolrException(SolrException.ErrorCode.BAD_REQUEST, "ConfigSet name not specified");
          }
          ZkConfigManager zkConfigManager = new ZkConfigManager(new CoreContainer().getZkController());
          if (zkConfigManager.configExists(newConfigSetName)) {
            throw new SolrException(SolrException.ErrorCode.BAD_REQUEST, "ConfigSet already exists: " + newConfigSetName);
          }
          if (!zkConfigManager.configExists(baseConfigSetName)) {
            throw new SolrException(SolrException.ErrorCode.BAD_REQUEST, "Base ConfigSet does not exist: " + baseConfigSetName);
          }
          if (!DISABLE_CREATE_AUTH_CHECKS &&
                  !isTrusted(req, new CoreContainer().getAuthenticationPlugin()) &&
                  isCurrentlyTrusted(new CoreContainer().getZkController(), "/configs/" + baseConfigSetName)) {
            throw new SolrException(SolrException.ErrorCode.UNAUTHORIZED,
                "Can't create a configset with an unauthenticated request from a trusted baseConfigSet");
          }
          Map<String, Object> props = CollectionsHandler.copy(req.getParams().required(), null, "name");
          props.put("baseConfigSet", baseConfigSetName);
          return copyPropertiesWithPrefix(req.getParams(), props, "property.");
        }
      };

      String action;
      ConfigSetOperation(String action) { this.action = action; }
      abstract Map<String, Object> call(SolrQueryRequest req, SolrQueryResponse rsp, ConfigSetsHandler h) throws Exception;
      static ConfigSetOperation get(String action) { return CREATE_OP; }
    }
  }
  ```

